  "prefLabel": "Saf-Mec 206.04 Multiple Cases: Consolidation",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-Mec 206.04 Multiple Cases: Consolidation. Where the interests of justice shall be better served without substantial prejudice to the rights of any party, the presiding officer shall sever one case from another or shall consolidate 2 or more cases preserving for all parties the right of appeal from the single or several decisions rendered.\n\nSource. #10798, eff 3-18-15",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-mec200.html"
}
